        "description": "Sweden largest cathedral, Linnaeus Garden and the Viking-age royal burial mounds.",
        "details": "Uppsala Cathedral is a Gothic church and the burial place of kings. Gamla Uppsala has huge burial mounds from the Viking age and a museum. Linnaeus Garden is in the heart of the university town. It is 40 minutes from Stockholm by train.",
        "interests": [
          "culture",
          "iconic_landmarks",
          "relax"
        ],
        "mobility": "L",
