        "name": "Gothenburg Haga, Liseberg and seafood",
        "description": "Wooden-house districts, canals, a big amusement park and fresh fish.",
        "details": "Gothenburg has the Haga district of cafes with huge cinnamon buns, the Feskekorka fish hall and Liseberg amusement park. Trams and canal boats link everything. The Southern Archipelago is reached by tram and ferry from Saltholmen.",
        "interests": [
          "food",
          "culture",
          "relax",
          "photography"
        ],
        "mobility": "L",
        "image": null
      },
      "sweden/gothenburg-archipelago": {
        "name": "Gothenburg southern archipelago",
        "description": "Car-free islands reached by tram and ferry, with rocky swimming spots.",
        "details": "Take tram 11 to Saltholmen and a ferry to Styrso or Branno. Islands are car-free and quiet, with lunch spots and bathing rocks. Ferries are part of the city travel ticket. It is a lovely day trip in summer.",
        "interests": [
          "relax",
